<p>Andrew E. Thorberg was born May 20, 1857, in Ronberg, Norway, into a family of two brothers and three sisters. Although the family immigrated to the United States, Andrew traveled alone to Davenport, Iowa, in 1876. He worked and attended school for a year while learning English.</p>

<p>Thorberg set out for the West Coast in 1878 but instead joined the Northern Pacific survey crew platting the new town of Mandan in Dakota Territory. Satisfied with the Missouri Slope, he remained after the survey ended. He initially worked as a trapper, becoming familiar with the region's land and resources. His observations of local soils and plants shaped his later interests.</p>

<div class="image-gallery">
